<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad Amin (naib of Shamil)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1901</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad Amin was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avar</a> religious leader sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam-shamil">Imam Shamil</a> in 1848 as his naib, or deputy, to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/circassians">Circassians</a> of the north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>. Among the Abadzekhs he built a more centralised Islamic administration with courts, taxes and a standing force. He submitted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in 1859 and later settled in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, where he died.</p></div>
